From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: monitor and invalidate NPU lifecycle owners

Latch owner invalidation before closing hardware admission routes. Defer
transaction drain to a retrying worker and require explicit renewal before
reusing authorization. Monitor open firmware state without reopening gates.
Cancel the owner worker before freeing its lifetime.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_bank1_routes.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_bank1_routes.h
@@ -31,6 +31,19 @@
 	routes->revoked = true;
 	routes->ready = false;
 	return airoha_bank1_routes_write_all(eth, true);
+}
+
+int airoha_bank1_routes_revoke(struct airoha_eth *eth, const void *owner)
+{
+	int error;
+
+	if (!eth || !owner)
+		return -EINVAL;
+	spin_lock_bh(&eth->ct_route_lock);
+	error = eth->ct_bank1_routes.owner == owner ?
+		airoha_bank1_routes_revoke_locked(eth) : -ESTALE;
+	spin_unlock_bh(&eth->ct_route_lock);
+	return error;
 }
 
